      "proofProvenance": "The universal symmetric-state bound is S4 ≥ C(10,4)/5 = 42. The threshold supplement supplies an exact four-term state with probabilities 23/126, 3/7, 1/6 and 2/9 on Dicke indices 0,3,6,9. Its second and fourth diagonal spin moments equal the uniform-spin values, while the specified phases cancel the only possible rank-four off-diagonal component. Thus a2=a4=0 and the lower bound is attained. An independent exact calculation from reduced purities also gives S4=42.",
